#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0370 expect=violation domain=CO
# Rule:Description: Part C - Raise and error when IDVAR in CO is not populated with a valid variable from the dataset referenced in RDOMAIN.
#note "CO IDVAR is spelled usubjid in lower case; the referenced RDOMAIN (DM) carries USUBJID. An IDVAR cell is a string value and compares exactly against the referenced dataset's column names, as every string does (owner ruling 2026-09-28, register CIT §3) -> usubjid is not one of DM's variables to this rule -> violation on row 1. That IDVAR should name the variable in its upper-case spelling is the naming rules' business."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 IDVAR=usubjid
dataset CO label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RDOMAIN type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col IDVAR type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col COVAL type=Char label="Comment"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | CO | 01-701-1015 | DM | usubjid | 01-701-1015 | Subject comment
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015
---
